  "generated_text": "The solution provided is correct. Let's break it down again for clarity:\n\n1. **Identify the prime numbers on a six-sided die:**\n   The numbers are \\(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\).\n   The prime numbers are \\(2, 3, 5\\).\n\n2. **Identify the non-prime numbers on a six-sided die:**\n   The non-prime numbers are \\(1, 4, 6\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the probability of not rolling a prime number on a single die:**\n   There are 3 non-prime numbers out of 6 possible outcomes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability of not rolling a prime number on one die} = \\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the probability of not rolling a prime number on both dice:**\n   Since the rolls are independent, we multiply the probabilities:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability of not rolling a prime number on both dice} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that Adam did not roll a prime number on either die is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\).",
