    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Adam rolled two standard six-sided dice once.  What is the probability that he did not roll a prime number on either die? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n\nThink step by step inside <think> </think> tags, then give your final answer inside \\boxed{}."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To determine the probability that Adam did not roll a prime number on either die when he rolled two standard six-sided dice, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the prime numbers on a six-sided die:**\n   The numbers on a standard six-sided die are \\(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\).\n   The prime numbers among these are \\(2, 3, 5\\).\n\n2. **Identify the non-prime numbers on a six-sided die:**\n   The non-prime numbers are \\(1, 4, 6\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the probability of not rolling a prime number on a single die:**\n   There are 3 non-prime numbers out of 6 possible outcomes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability of not rolling a prime number on one die} = \\frac{\\text{Number of non-prime numbers}}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}} = \\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the probability of not rolling a prime number on both dice:**\n   Since the rolls of the two dice are independent events, we multiply the probabilities of each event.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability of not rolling a prime number on both dice} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that Adam did not roll a prime number on either die is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)."
    },
